## What We Shipped (4 commits, all verified tsc 0 / vitest 1089 / replay-pilot 30)

1. **`bab7a7f`** — de-accrete Polina's system prompt (`lib/concierge/system-prompt-builder.ts`).
   The prompt was a "scar-museum": ~6 rules all saying "act don't announce", ~4 "drive don't wait",
   THREE incident-named BANNED-PHRASE catalogs (TD-34/46.b/47.b). Collapsed to positive one-liners,
   deleted the catalogs, kept the DATA (gate chain, tool-pickers, ID-discipline). Fixed the
   "You are running on OpenAI model" lie (now model-neutral). −14.4k chars (~3.6k tokens). ONE prompt,
   no per-model fork. Tests updated to assert invariants not scar-text.

2. **`b8eb6b8`** — E13 shot-id unblock. Root cause (VERIFIED, not legacy data): stale examples in
   concierge TOOL SCHEMAS (`tools/eref-execute.ts:71`, `vgen-execute.ts:71/224`, `shot-reorder.ts:108`)
   showed the pre-refactor compound `SS-S15-E01-A2-SC04-SH08`; Polina (small model) copied it →
   `SS-S15-E13-A1-SC01-SH03` → `getStoryboardShotById` exact-match failed vs new-format STB. Fix:
   (A) tool examples → `SH08`/`S15-E13-SH08`; (B) `resolveShotId` (`lib/api/shot-id.ts`) now EXTRACTS
   `S{s}-E{e}-SH{n}` from any compound (strips SS-/A/SC) — entry-door canonicalisation, NOT the deleted
   comparison-site band-aid; (C) Polina BEHAVIOR_CONTRACT rule "missing precondition = a step, not a
   question". WORKED live: SH03/SH04 got Shot Plans, CREAD ran.

3. **`30b0143`** — kill false `pickup_timeout` alarms (`lib/concierge/tools/wait-for-pickup.ts`).
   Root cause: a `jobs` row is inserted only when a function BODY starts (jobs has only RUNNING/
   COMPLETED, no QUEUED); under a saturated batch a queued job has no row for >10s → false hard-fail
   "work NOT started / Inngest down". Fix: on timeout, check worker LIVENESS (any RUNNING job or any
   job in last ~3min) → alive = advisory "queued, will run shortly" (no q27); dead = keep the real
   alarm. One central helper (all 5 dispatch tools). 2 new tests.

4. **`e0c5e3f`** — #5 one-attempt (`inngest/functions/exec-cread.ts`). CREAD is the TASTE critic;
   its storyboard phase was already advisory (q15). Extended to per-shot eref/vanim phases: REVISE no
   longer re-fires the producer — attempt-1 ships, verdict surfaces as advisory (REV-readability +
   warning row). CANON critics (EPREV/VPREV/WCHK) STILL BLOCK ("если не канон"). SREV left as-is.
   Deleted the per-shot re-author dispatch (subtractive).

