## The Big "Why" Diagnoses (partnership session — Director asked me to THINK/critique)

- **Polina cost** = model-tier × prompt-size(29k) × volume. Free makes tier=$0 → total $0 regardless of
  who pushes. The bomb only exists on a paid tier + fat prompt. Director noticed Opus≈free quality
  BECAUSE when he drives, HE is the brain; her job is routing (needs reliable tool-calling, not a
  frontier model). The 29k prompt was tuned for gpt-5.5/Sonnet-era incidents → noise for gemini-flash.
- **Polina "knows but asks"** (q24 hedge) = calibration on a small model + a missing positive rule
  (fixed in `b8eb6b8` part C). She still needs occasional nudges; the de-accretion helped ("получше").
- **Who ate the API (budget_log 48h):** EXEC-EREF $43.6 (images, gpt-image-2/OpenAI) + EXEC-VGEN $39.6
  (video, fal) = $83 of $118 — NOT Anthropic. Anthropic = text designers EREF-DESIGNER $10.5 + VANIM
  $3.5. EXEC-CONC $17.8 is PHANTOM (she's on free; cost.ts prices every model with Anthropic rates —
  known bug). So "move designers to free" saves ~$14 and risks canon drift — NOT worth it; #5 hits the $83.
- **Reject/select bugs** = the ref is auto-APPROVED (REGENERATE_EXHAUSTED); the drawer's Approve/Reject
  are built for the REVIEW→decision flow, semantically wrong for an already-APPROVED ref.

